## TL;DR — 60-Second Answer

**The 4 GIA cert fields that save $2,000 on a marquise diamond:**

1. **Color grade** — G-H is the marquise sweet spot; D-F adds $800–$1,400 for improvement invisible in a marquise setting
2. **Clarity grade** — VS2 is the ceiling for marquise; VVS2 costs $1,079–$2,095 more with zero visible difference
3. **Measurements** — divide Length ÷ Width from the mm dimensions; 1.85–2.00:1 is the ideal range; outside it, you pay for a shape buyers don't want
4. **Table % and Depth %** — depth over 62% shrinks face-up area; a 1ct stone cut at 64% depth looks like a 0.9ct stone on the finger

**The real $2,000 example from certified market inventory:**
- [1ct F VS2 Ideal GIA marquise — $4,473](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29764389?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- [1ct F VVS2 Ideal GIA marquise — $6,568](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29719954?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- **Difference: $2,095.** Same color. Same cut. One clarity grade apart. Zero visible difference on the finger.

