## Fluorescence: The Fifth Field Worth Checking

The GIA cert also lists Fluorescence. For marquise, fluorescence is a secondary consideration — but it can lower price.

A marquise with Strong or Very Strong fluorescence is often listed 10–20% below market. Same color and clarity, lower price. In most lighting, fluorescence has no visible effect. In UV-heavy light — office lighting, direct sunlight — strong fluorescence can make the stone look milky.

For H-I color, faint or medium blue fluorescence can improve appearance. It offsets the stone's natural warmth. Dealers call this "beneficial fluorescence."

**Practical rule:** For D-F color marquise, avoid strong fluorescence. For G-I color, faint or medium blue is fine and often lowers price. Check this line on the GIA cert before finalizing.

## How to Read a GIA Report on a Retailer Listing

On Blue Nile, every GIA-certified stone links directly to the GIA report. Here is the sequence:

1. Use the marquise filter: [Browse GIA Certified Marquise](https://www.bluenile.com/diamonds?Shape=marquise-cut&CertificateToggle=yes&Lab=GIA&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
2. Click any stone to open the detail page
3. Click "View GIA Report" — this opens the official GIA PDF
4. Check: Measurements (calculate L/W), Table %, Depth %, Polish, Symmetry, Fluorescence
5. Compare stones side by side at your target grade

The measurements calculation takes 10 seconds. Divide Length by Width. If the result is between 1.85 and 2.00, the stone is classically proportioned. If it's outside that range, consider whether the price reflects that unusual shape.

The depth and table check is one line in the proportion section. Under 62% depth and 53–63% table — buy with confidence on proportions. Over those numbers — verify further before buying.

## Lab-Grown GIA Marquise Diamonds

[Lab-grown marquise diamonds](/lab-grown-marquise-diamond) are graded by GIA using the same Clarity and Color scales. The lab cert looks identical to a natural cert. The only difference is a statement identifying the stone as laboratory-grown.

Lab marquise diamonds with GIA reports are available across certified retailer inventory. They carry the same 4Cs grades as natural, at 40–70% lower prices.

All four cert fields apply equally to lab stones:
- Color sweet spot for lab marquise: G-H in white metal, H-I in yellow gold
- Clarity ceiling: VS2 (same logic — VVS2 adds cost with no visible benefit)
- Measurements L/W ratio: 1.85–2.00:1 same target
- Table % and Depth %: same proportion targets

Pairing with a [marquise diamond wedding band](/marquise-diamond-wedding-band)? VS2 clarity and G-H color still apply. The pairing doesn't change what the cert should show.

Browse certified lab marquise (GIA, IGI, GCAL): [Lab-Grown Marquise Diamonds](https://www.bluenile.com/diamonds/lab-grown-diamonds?Shape=marquise-cut&CertificateToggle=yes&Lab=GIA,IGI,GCAL&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

